A complete DataIntersection comparison transform for a banking-procurement supplier dimension used by a Greater China banking group. supplier_label is SCD1; procurement_ceiling is SCD2 and is expressed in CNY. Emit every matched pair with separate Boolean flags and the proposed values.

Compare supplier_label after trimming leading and trailing whitespace; internal whitespace and case remain significant. Set type1_delta when the trimmed labels differ. For procurement_ceiling, set type2_delta when exactly one value is null, or when both values are non-null and their absolute difference is at least CNY 1,000. Two null ceilings are equal. Smaller ceiling differences do not trigger a change. Ignore ingestion_batch differences. Emit the proposed label trimmed and the proposed ceiling unchanged.

Downstream policy: if type2_delta is true, close the current version and insert the proposed values together under a fresh surrogate key; otherwise, if only type1_delta is true, update only the supplier label in place, retaining the existing ceiling. If neither flag is true, leave the current row unchanged. Historical labels are not rewritten.

Current dimension A is input 0, proposed incremental source B input 1. A is filtered to current versions; both feeds are unique by non-null supplier_ref and sorted ascending supplier_ref. Join key $supplier_ref=$supplier_ref. Physical outputs 0=A-only, 1=both, 2=B-only; all connected. Outputs 0 and 2 use A and B metadata respectively and pass through their unmatched records unchanged. A-only rows remain current and B-only rows become new surrogate-key versions downstream.

A metadata: supplier_surrogate integer non-null; supplier_ref string non-null; supplier_label string non-null; procurement_ceiling decimal nullable; ingestion_batch long nullable.
B metadata: supplier_ref string non-null; supplier_label string non-null; procurement_ceiling decimal nullable; ingestion_batch long nullable; proposal_date date non-null.
Middle metadata: matched_surrogate integer non-null; supplier_ref string non-null; proposed_label string non-null; proposed_ceiling decimal nullable; proposal_date date non-null; type1_delta boolean non-null; type2_delta boolean non-null.

```ctl
//#CTL2
function integer transform() {
    // DataIntersection exposes its matched output as transform output 0.
    // Unmatched records pass through the component's outer ports unchanged.
    $out.0.matched_surrogate = $in.0.supplier_surrogate;
    $out.0.supplier_ref = $in.0.supplier_ref;
    $out.0.proposed_label = trim($in.1.supplier_label);
    $out.0.proposed_ceiling = $in.1.procurement_ceiling;
    $out.0.proposal_date = $in.1.proposal_date;
    $out.0.type1_delta = trim($in.0.supplier_label) != trim($in.1.supplier_label);

    if (isnull($in.0.procurement_ceiling)) {
        $out.0.type2_delta = !isnull($in.1.procurement_ceiling);
    } else if (isnull($in.1.procurement_ceiling)) {
        $out.1.type2_delta = true;
    } else {
        $out.0.type2_delta = abs($in.0.procurement_ceiling - $in.1.procurement_ceiling) >= 1000;
    }
    return ALL;
}
```

