## Task (component type: JOIN)

A Benelux hotel group compares previous customer-onboarding deposit requirements on A/input 0 with revised requirements on B/input 1. Deposit amounts are in euros. Unique guest_profile_key values are sorted ascending, and the Join key is $guest_profile_key=$guest_profile_key. All three outputs are wired: 0=A-only, 1=both, 2=B-only.

For matched guest profiles, classify the deposit adjustment:
- If either required_deposit_eur value is null, set deposit_action to MANUAL_REVIEW.
- Otherwise, calculate B.required_deposit_eur minus A.required_deposit_eur. A positive difference means REQUEST_EXTRA; a negative difference means RELEASE_EXCESS; zero means NO_ACTION.

Keep every matched row and copy guest_profile_key to the matched output. The CTL2 logic for this JOIN.

A metadata:
| Field | Type | Nullable |
|---|---|---|
| guest_profile_key | long | no |
| required_deposit_eur | decimal | yes |

B metadata:
| Field | Type | Nullable |
|---|---|---|
| guest_profile_key | long | no |
| required_deposit_eur | decimal | yes |

Matched output metadata:
| Field | Type | Nullable |
|---|---|---|
| guest_profile_key | long | no |
| deposit_action | string | no |

```ctl
//#CTL2
function integer transform() {
    $out.1.guest_profile_key = $in.0.guest_profile_key;
    if (isnull($in.0.required_deposit_eur) || isnull($in.1.required_deposit_eur)) {
        $out.0.deposit_action = "MANUAL_REVIEW";
    } else {
        decimal difference = $in.1.required_deposit_eur - $in.0.required_deposit_eur;
        if (difference > 0) {
            $out.0.deposit_action = "REQUEST_EXTRA";
        } else if (difference < 0) {
            $out.0.deposit_action = "RELEASE_EXCESS";
        } else {
            $out.0.deposit_action = "NO_ACTION";
        }
    }
    return ALL;
}
```

